  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Blind Watten (Ladinisch Watten). 4 players, partnerships. 33-card German deck + WELI. 5 tricks. Trumps chosen SECRETLY: forehand shows rank (Schlag) to dealer, dealer shows suit to forehand. Partners must deduce. No signals. Guate > Rechte > Linken > trumps. Betting to raise stakes. South Tyrolean.',
    Player: "You're the dealer's partner. First trick: forehand leads the Ober of Hearts. Dealer plays the 7 of Bells. You see the dealer was NOT forced to follow with a trump — so Hearts is probably NOT the trump suit, and the Ober is probably not the Schlag. What do you play?",
    objective: 'Win at least three out of five tricks to win the hand. First team to 15 or 18 points wins the match.',
    gameplay: "1. **Secret Selection**: Forehand and dealer establish rank and suit trumps in secret. 2. **Play**: Forehand leads. **Must Follow Suit** only applies to forehand and dealer for trumps. Partners have no follow obligation but must try to deduce trumps. 3. **The Cards**: Highest card is the 'Guate' (Schlag + 1), followed by the 'Rechte' (Schlag in trump suit), then the 'Linken' (Schlag in the other suit of same color).",
    keyRules: [
      'No signals or verbal communication allowed between partners.',
      "The first trick's cards remain face up on the table to assist in deduction.",
      'WELI is always bells unless 6 is the Schlag.',
      'Betting (raising the stakes) can be done at any time during the hand.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: true,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: '4 players in two fixed partnerships (North-South vs East-West).',
      deck: '33 cards: A, K, O, U, 10, 9, 8, 7 in four suits plus the WELI (6 of Bells).',
      equipment: 'German-suited deck, score pad.',
      dealing: 'Deal 5 cards to each player. Forehand shows a card rank (Schlag) to the dealer in secret; the dealer shows a suit back to forehand in secret.',
    },
    turnFlow: "1. **Secret Selection**: Forehand and dealer establish rank and suit trumps in secret. 2. **Play**: Forehand leads. **Must Follow Suit** only applies to forehand and dealer for trumps. Partners have no follow obligation but must try to deduce trumps. 3. **The Cards**: Highest card is the 'Guate' (Schlag + 1), followed by the 'Rechte' (Schlag in trump suit), then the 'Linken' (Schlag in the other suit of same color).",
    moveValidityConditions: {
      ante: 'Blind Watten is a point-based partnership game and does not utilize a monetary or chip-based ante.',
      deal: 'The initial distribution of five cards to each of the four players is performed automatically by the system dealer.',
      reveal_market: 'This is a closed-hand game where all cards are dealt to players; no public market or shared pool exists.',
      buy_market: 'Players cannot purchase or swap cards from any external area; they must succeed with their initial hand.',
      buy_stock: 'The entire 20 cards in play are distributed at the start; no cards remain in stock to be purchased.',
      fold: 'Participation is mandatory for every trick until the round concludes to determine the point winner.',
      check: 'The game uses a trick-taking structure rather than a vying structure where checking would be an appropriate action.',
      call: 'There is no central pot to match in this game; competition is based on trick wins and raised stakes.',
      bet: 'Success is determined by trick accumulation on a scorecard rather than through financial or chip betting.',
      raise: 'Allowed during the play of any trick before the showdown.',
      declare: 'Trumps are established through a secret showing phase rather than a formal declaration or bidding.',
      reveal_hand: 'Hands stay private until individual cards are played into tricks; no full-hand reveal phase occurs.',
      award_pot: 'Winning points are added to a cumulative partnership total rather than awarded from a physical pot.',
      play_card: 'Must follow suit if forehand or dealer and trump is led.',
      draw: 'Each player receives five cards at the start and no further drawing occurs during the play of the hand.',
      discard: 'Every card in the hand must be played into a trick; no cards are discarded to a waste pile.',
      pass: 'Allowed when an opponent proposes a stake increase.',
      bid: 'Trump selection is performed via a secret showing phase rather than a competitive bidding auction.',
      meld: 'Blind Watten is strictly a trick-taking game based on card ranks rather than forming melds.',
      go_out: 'The hand terminates only after all five tricks have been played by all participants.',
    },
    exampleHands: [
      'Opening deal: 4-4 player(s), 5 card(s) per player, 1 deck(s), initial visibility face_down.',
      'Opening flow: start in dealing; system may use deal_5_each before secret_selection.',
      'Scoring check: Win 3+ of 5 tricks = 2 points (or higher if stakes were raised by betting). First team to target score wins. Expected outcome: 15.',
